  "faithful": "29. The days indulged by law to a defender, between his citation and appearance, to prepare for his defence, are called inducie legales. If he is within the kingdom, twenty one and fix days, for the first and second diets of appearance, must be allowed him for that purpose; and if out of it, sixty and fifteen. Defenders residing in Orkney or Zetland must be cited on forty days. In certain summonses which are privileged, the inducie are shortened: Spuilzies and ejections proceed on fifteen days; wakening",
